WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.980
Being together like this...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.310
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.830
...under this sky...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.440
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.130
In this beauty...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.240
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.290
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.420
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.010
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.080
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.080
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.940
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.640
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.740
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.390
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.520
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.600
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
If you go there...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.830
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.210
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.340
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.590
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.780
Under this sky...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
...we'll walk together!

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.800
I'm terribly sorry, Sir Anubis.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.010
At Kaluiza, they noticed our existence.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.390
And last time, we were almost caught.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.110
If the higher-ups find out about this; you'll be killed.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.320
You still have a chance.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:01:59.570
This is...

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.990
We've kidnapped this person.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:10.210
If a double were to sneak into DDS under your orders... then...

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.640
Hongou-kun, is it OK for you to be out of the hospital?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.480
You made me spend a month in the there for a Few scratches.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.940
I can go back to work any time.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:33.270
All the same to think I'll be teaching here at DDS...

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.280
Now, don't say that.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.860
DDS is what will bring forth the next generation of
detectives to carry on my Dan's Detective Agency.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.120
It's an important organization.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.410
I called you to teach out of the respect for your abilities.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:51.000
Oh, and your former classmate Nanami-kun is here as well...

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.000
Please don't associate me with him.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.460
Anyways its already been decided.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.180
For at least awhile, please do your best to train our pupils.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.090
Yes sir.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.810
Now our staff is back in full swing.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:13.310
Maki-sensei is back from overseas and she's ready to resume her forensics class.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.940
Now that Pluto's Shadow is beginning to surface,

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.740
I'll need everyone to be more diligent than ever.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.370
A new teacher?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.080
Seems like it.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.420
My intuition tells me that it'll be a really hot babe.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.590
What do you think she'll teach us?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.630
The forbidden love between a beautiful teacher and her student...

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.930
Teacher.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.550
What are you talking about?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.260
Dan-sensei?

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:52.640
Let me introduce to you,

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.110
this is our new teacher for Q Class.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.230
Hongou Tatsumi.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:02.910
DDS Teacher, Hongou Tatsumi

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.030
I'm Hongou.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.530
Nice to meet you.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.200
Pretty scary, huh?

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.000
He looks more like an assassin than a teacher.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.250
You two!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.790
No whispering!

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.170
We're sorry.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.840
Now then, I've got a meeting to attend to, I'll be going

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.510
Hongou-sensei, sorry for the short notice, but take care of the class.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.270
Let me say to begin with.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.610
Having finally met you, I'm disappointed.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.650
From the look on your faces

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.950
I can tell that you don't have the slightest bit of readiness to be detectives.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.500
If the top class of DDS is like this,

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:57.460
I can understand why Dan-sensei called me here.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.170
Why you...

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.420
And you think I'll just listen while you talk crap about us?

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:03.670
You with the ponytail.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.050
You seem to have an issue with this.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.010
If you've got a problem, then speak up.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.560
Hongou-sensei, please start the lesson.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.020
I see...

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.900
1 guess at least one of you might be qualified.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:27.160
Are you the one who passed with 100% on the DDS entry exam?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.910
Amakusa Ryuu.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:30.910
Nice to meet you.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:38.540
But avoiding eye contact when you speak to other people...
You're acting more like a criminal than a detective.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.010
I'm Kyuu.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.550
Nice to meet you.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:54.020
Minami Megumi, nice to meet you.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.980
Narasawa Kazuma.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.640
Nice to meet you.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.360
Kouyama Kintarou.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.020
Nice to meet you

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.320
I'll begin the class then

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:10.910
Today, we're going to talk about trailing someone.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.700
Open yours books to page 37.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.210
It's Finally over.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.840
Today was twice as tiring as normal.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.220
Maybe I'll have Kaidou come pick me up...

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:32.470
But it's true that he's a very experienced detective

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:34.970
How can you tell?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.770
The watch on his left hand is large and scratched.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:44.230
And his hand, from fingers to wrist, is covered with blade marks.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.570
There's only one reason why a detective would wear a heavy watch.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.950
It's to be able to block a criminal's blade with his hands in case of an attack.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.870
The watch protects the artery on his wrist.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:57.660
Block blades with his bare hands?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.460
What?

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:04.210
And that stupid face of his proves that he was a failure as a detective.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.840
K-Kinta!

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.470
W-We I, I have to get to work, see ya!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:18.140
I forgot to mention it, but this room and the entire building is a mess.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.150
Having a polished training environment is the basis of learning.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:27.610
You're going to clean up the place everyday after class.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:32.360
And today it I'll be you, Ponytail.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:33.200
All right?

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.580
Y - Yes sir.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.790
I want to have the documents room downstairs sparkle.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.580
Ah, dammit.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.580
I've got work today!

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.550
Please, can one of you do it instead?

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.880
I really can't miss work today.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.590
If I do, I'll be fired.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.380
OK, bye guys.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:57.640
Why you... He just went home without saying anything?

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.020
But you guys wouldn't be that cold, right?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.600
I can't.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.730
I already called for a ride

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:05.980
Bye.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.230
Dammit...

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.910
Kyuu, Kyuu-san, please?!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:13.490
See ya!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:15.820
Please take care of it!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.580
Hey, Kinta!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.960
Jeez... I guess I have no choice

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.000
Oh, it'll be fine.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.830
I'll stay behind too.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.750
Let's help him out today.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:28.500
Together?

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.880
With two of us, it'll be done in no time, right?

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.970
Yeah, that's right.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.010
Documents Room

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.600
Here it is.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.390
Wow, It's really dusty.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.150
It's like one of those weird rooms in a mystery novel.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.400
So I guess Hongou-sensei's really starting to work you, huh?

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:52.900
Dan-sensei?

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:54.910
Katagiri-sensei?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.160
A murder?

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.240
A person was killed here?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:05.370
Yes, it was when I first rented the place.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.250
I heard about it later,

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.170
but this was the crime scene of a very sad death.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.880
A murder scene...

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:20.560
When I learned about it, I realized that my life was going
to revolve around murders wherever I would go.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.940
Well, don't take too long.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.810
There's rumors that a ghost appears

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.230
My, Dan-sensei...

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.910
Ho way... A ghost?

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:38.620
Right, Megu?

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.160
1 think... I'll go home!

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.240
Hey, wait!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.210
I'm tired...

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.630
All the sweeping and cleaning is done.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.380
Hey, isn't this is a map of the building?

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:54.050
1936.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.510
That's Showa Year, 11.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.300
The name of the person who designed it is written here.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:00.550
You're right.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.020
Kazuryuu Takumi?

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.980
That's a strange name.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.310
OK, break's over.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.480
Get some water and we'll mop the place.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.030
OK, I'll go fill the bucket.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.030
I'll take the trash out.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:22.660
Oh no!

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.250
The bottom of the shelf is all wet.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.120
What's wrong?

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.290
Megu, can you help me move this?

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:35.760
OK.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.020
There was a door here? I had no idea...

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.980
I don't remember seeing it on the map.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.480
It won't open

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.690
Let's look at it from the outside.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.410
It's not here.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:08.040
Do you think it might be connected to this storeroom?

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:09.500
Maybe.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:15.800
Nothing...

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.970
It's just a wall.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.760
There isn't a door anywhere.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.350
Why'd they do something so weird?

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.560
That Kuzuryuu guy who built the place...

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:28.060
Huh?

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:29.600
What's wrong, Megu?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.400
This wall is strange.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.400
I think there's a room inside.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:34.310
What?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:39.280
You're right.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:40.400
I get it...

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:42.450
Then...

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:48.200
Maybe there's a hidden room in this storehouse, and that door, leads to it?

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.580
But it's too small for a room.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.750
From what we saw outside, it's got to be only a meter or so long.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.310
Dammit... If we can only open the door.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.230
We might learn a secret about the building
that even Dan-sensei doesn't even know.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.730
Come on, Kyuu it's dark

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:15.980
Let's go home and do it tomorrow.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:20.240
No... If I go home now, I'll spend the whole night thinking about it.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.990
There's got to be a secret beyond this door.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.040
These pictures of dragons...

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.330
There are 10 of them.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:37.500
Kuzuryuu, the man who built the building,
his name means "9 Dragons”, right?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.670
So why are there 10 here?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.930
Now that you mention it...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:50.850
If the pictures are supposed to represent his name then there should only be 9.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.980
Could there really only be 9 of them?

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.070
Huh? What do you mean?

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:03.030
These 10 dragons are all evenly spaced, right?

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.030
There's a mark here!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:10.700
This goes like this ..this part goes...

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.450
I get it!

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:15.460
Like this...

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:25.630
10 dragons turned into 9.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.010
This door itself is a trick puzzle that uses the dragon's.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:00.980
It opened.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.400
This is...

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:08.570
I knew it.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.950
This door is an entrance to the basement.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:14.370
Let's go.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:15.330
What?

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:16.700
You're going?

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.210
We should go call a teacher or something...

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.080
I'll go myself.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:23.590
Then you wait there.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.170
Me alone?

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.590
Hey, don't leave me here alone!

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:35.060
Kyuu!

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:42.230
Kyuu...

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:43.650
Oh, right.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.110
We can use the Flashlight in the DDS Kit...

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.820
It's another door.

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:55.530
It's got a really strong bar lock on it.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:58.120
What's this?

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.210
Isn't that where they slide food through?

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:05.960
In movies and stuff you see them sliding food to prisoners this way.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:09.300
A cell...

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:10.550
OK?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:11.130
Wait.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.260
Let's stop.

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.800
I've got a bad feeling.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:18.560
What? You look so serious...

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.270
Ghosts don’t exist.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:22.850
That's not it!

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.650
Getting scared of something like this just
means you won't cut it as a detective.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:28.270
Fine.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:29.690
Let's go.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:32.450
I'm a member of Q Class too.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:34.320
OK, then it's decided.

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:52.260
It's really musty in here!

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.300
This is... A broken chamber pot?

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:01.390
Somebody really was locked up in here.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.190
There's another door.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.150
What?

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:09.690
You're still going?

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:10.900
OF course!

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:17.780
Let's go.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:22.040
<i>Kyuu can just grab onto a girl's hand like it’s nothing.</i>

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.620
<i>Is he just a kid?</i>

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:30.090
<i>Or does he not even think I'm a girl?</i>

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:39.970
It's small.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:43.600
But there's no doubt someone was in here.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:49.980
They slept with this battered blanket...

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:52.400
A plate?

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.280
Did they eat out of that?

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.570
There's a shattered cup too.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:01.620
Who do think was locked up in here?

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:09.380
Dan-sensei said he learned about the murder after he started renting the place.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:11.670
All right.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:16.800
Put on your crime scene gloves.

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:24.390
It's a bit old but it may have something to do with the murder scene.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:28.650
Let's put on our gloves on so we don't smudge anything

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:33.190
You've gotten into it too, Megu!

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.210
What's wrong Kyuu?

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:50.670
A chopstick...

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:52.670
The tip is black.

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:57.630
Did they whittle it down and used it as a pen?

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.390
It looks like there's ink or something on it.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:01.970
Could that be...

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:07.180
Let's use the luminole from our detective notebooks.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.860
Then this "ink" on the end could be...

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.440
Show me the tip.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.830
It glowed! That's a luminole reaction!

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:25.620
Then it really is blood!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:30.500
They used blood in place of ink to write something...

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:32.670
But what?

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.750
It might be a diary!

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:37.010
Diary?

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:42.640
If you spent all your time in the darkness, you'd lose track of time.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:47.720
I'd be really afraid if that happened, I'd definitely keep a diary.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.690
Then there should be remnants of it...

00:18:58.800 --> 00:18:59.650
Bingo.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:03.570
It's a diary written on some kind of paper...

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.490
All right!

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:08.700
I'm so excited!

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.120
April 7th.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:14.130
I awaken from a nightmare.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:19.380
1 don't even know if it's morning or night.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:43.320
How long can I survive in this darkness?

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:51.290
Yet, the food comes through my small window like always, so it must be dawn.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:54.330
Today it's bread, a can of meat, and water.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.670
They must want to let me live.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.090
What does that mean...?

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:13.230
I'll kill you.

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:17.270
I'll get out of here...

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.660
Did you hear something back in the hall?

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:36.580
Maybe someone's coming.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.130
Hey, let's go back.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:41.960
We've found out enough.

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:43.920
Y-You're right, Megu.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.310
Was that door shut before?

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:53.390
No, I didn't close it...

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:01.570
It won't open!

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:07.070
Dammit...

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:10.450
No way!

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.540
Stop kidding around, Kyuu!

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:13.450
Not at a time like this!

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:15.660
I'm not joking...

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.830
It really won't open.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:21.590
Then that noise before was the lock...

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:25.260
But it shouldn't be that easy to just lock it...

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:28.930
Hey, does that mean...

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:32.510
We're stuck in here?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.560
But someone will find us in the morning, right?

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:42.820
How?

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:47.740
If this door was deliberately shut by someone,

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:53.120
that means the doors up there are shut too.

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:58.000
And even Dan-sensei didn't notice that door...

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.880
Who's going to find it now?

00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:09.970
Hey!

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:11.260
Anybody!

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:13.890
Someone, save us!

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:15.220
Anyone!

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:18.980
It's no good.

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:21.940
Our voices won't even reach out to hallway!

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:24.860
What should we do?

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:30.410
I'm scared...

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:33.330
Whats wrong?

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:36.330
Something's at my feet...

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:43.290
That's a pit viper...

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:47.340
Dammit!

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:12.990
Kyuu...

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:15.450
Are you OK?

00:23:16.720 --> 00:23:17.580
What should we do?

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:20.750
I got bit...

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:23.040
...by that snake...

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:24.250
What?

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:28.630
At this rate... I'll die!

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:36.890
Megu

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.060
Detective Academy

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.420
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.760
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.090
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.100
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.390
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.930
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.730
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.980
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.610
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.700
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:16.120
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.240
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.790
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.670
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.880
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:30.380
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.340
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.260
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.640
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.470
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:46.420
The worries of Bunny Kinta!

00:24:47.810 --> 00:25:06.480
*Next Episode

00:24:48.650 --> 00:24:50.340
A sealed underground cell,

00:24:51.030 --> 00:24:53.710
and glimpses of Pluto's shadow.

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:56.880
The poison spreads through Megu's body.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:58.430
We're running out of time

00:24:59.080 --> 00:24:59.760
Think!

00:25:03.960 --> 00:25:05.020
There's only one answer!

00:25:07.500 --> 00:25:09.360
Bye bye, Bunny!

00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:19.200
What kind of sounds are bunnies supposed to make?
